  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive employment and skills policies and programmes developed and adopted</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO will support the Government in shaping a workforce that can advance Qatar&#x2019;s broader national social and economic strategy. This means ensuring Qatari nationals and migrant workers can meet the needs of the private sector, including in anticipation of major changes that are brought about by digitalization, technology, the green economy, evolving production modes as well as labour market functioning, etc. Skills development is a key element of this strategy, and it also requires that regulatory frameworks are more flexible in adjusting to diverse forms of employment and work organization arrangements. Flexible work arrangements are among a set of gender-responsive policies that also promote female labour force participation, with specific interventions targeting Qatari women. Critically, these workforce policies will be guided by a strong evidence base.</narrative>
  </description>
